ate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.07639906661579898,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":9.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04294956809841999,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":46.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.037957168868984696,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":53.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0312199653414722,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":89.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010328459601470373,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.03967,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":26.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Encore Capital Group, Inc., a specialty finance company, provides debt recovery solutions and other related services for consumers across financial assets worldwide. The company purchases portfolios of defaulted consumer receivables at discounts to face value, as well as manages them by working with individuals as they repay their obligations and works toward financial recovery. It is also involved in the provision of debt servicing, such as early stage collection, business process outsourcing, and contingent collection services. In addition, the company engages in debt servicing and other portfolio management services to credit originator for non-performing loans. Further, it offers credit management services. Encore Capital Group, Inc. was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ashish  Masih | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $241K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Encore Capital Group Inc is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.4B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $127M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.60\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 20% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Encore Capital Stock Jumps 26% on Stellar Q3 Earnings: Is ECPG a Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025612/encore-capital-stock-jumps-26-on-stellar-q3-earnings-is-ecpg-a-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Crank_focused-3025612","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793974440.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Encore Capital Group (ECPG) stock is up today","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/ecpg/news/why-up-down/why-encore-capital-group-ecpg-stock-is-up-today-2","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793912736.0,"origi